`text_html_urled` passes `urled=True` into `Message._parse_html`. The test constructs the text `alpha beta gamma https://x.y/z omega` with entities for bold on `alpha beta gamma`, nested italic on `beta`, nested code on `gamma`, and a URL on `https://x.y/z`. In `_parse_html`, the URL entity has no nested entities, so the `else` branch sets `escaped_text = escape(text)`, which leaves `https://x.y/z` unchanged. Because the entity type is `MessageEntity.URL` and `urled` is true, `insert` is built as `<a href="https://x.y/z">https://x.y/z</a>`. The returned `html_text` is the concatenation of the earlier bold-rendered segment, a space, that URL link, and the trailing ` omega`.

## Answer
{"escaped_text":"https://x.y/z","html_text":"<b>alpha <i>beta</i> <code>gamma</code></b> <a href=\"https://x.y/z\">https://x.y/z</a> omega","insert":"<a href=\"https://x.y/z\">https://x.y/z</a>"}
